# Tests for the Qualifying_relative module

Run with `clerk test`. Each named scope is one concrete person, worked by
hand from IRC 152(b), 152(d) and Pub. 501 (2024) pp 11, 18-19 as quoted in
`catala/qualifying_relative.catala_en`. Every scope sets satisfiable inputs
(a real person a real filer could enter) and asserts the expected result and
the rejection of the wrong one. The oracle comparison is
`make difftest-persons` (per-person Direct File values, `oracle/persons.csv`).

> Using Qualifying_child as Q
> Using Qualifying_relative as R

## Helper: a household member with default answers

The default is the filer's parent, born 1950-04-02 (74), a U.S. citizen with
an SSN, who lived with the filer for less than six months, had $3,000 of
gross income, did not provide over half of their own support, was supported
over half by the filer, is unmarried, and is nobody's qualifying child. The
filer (`oldest_filer_dob`) was born 1985-06-15, is a U.S. citizen, and cannot
be claimed by anyone. A test overrides only what it tests.

```catala
declaration scope MkMember:
  context relationship content Q.Relationship
  context date_of_birth content date
  context full_time_student content boolean
  context residency_duration content Q.ResidencyDuration
  context own_support content boolean
  context married content boolean
  context writable_joint_return content boolean
  context could_be_qc_of_another content boolean
  context potential_claimer_must_file content boolean
  context potential_claimer_did_file content boolean
  context gross_income content money
  context qr_support content boolean
  context tin_type content R.TinType
  context citizen content boolean
  context us_resident content boolean
  context us_national content boolean
  context canada_mexico_resident content boolean
  context tp_claims content boolean
  output member content R.Member

scope MkMember:
  definition relationship equals Q.Relationship.Parent
  definition date_of_birth equals |1950-04-02|
  definition full_time_student equals false
  definition residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition own_support equals false
  definition married equals false
  definition writable_joint_return equals false
  definition could_be_qc_of_another equals false
  definition potential_claimer_must_file equals false
  definition potential_claimer_did_file equals false
  definition gross_income equals $3,000
  definition qr_support equals true
  definition tin_type equals R.TinType.Ssn
  definition citizen equals true
  definition us_resident equals false
  definition us_national equals false
  definition canada_mexico_resident equals false
  definition tp_claims equals true
  definition member equals R.Member {
    -- person: Q.Person {
         -- relationship: relationship
         -- date_of_birth: date_of_birth
         -- full_time_student: full_time_student
         -- permanent_total_disability: false
         -- residency_duration: residency_duration
         -- own_support: own_support
         -- married: married
         -- writable_joint_return: writable_joint_return
         -- writable_required_to_file: false
         -- writable_filing_only_for_refund: false
         -- writable_could_be_qualifying_child_of_another: could_be_qc_of_another
         -- writable_potential_claimer_must_file: potential_claimer_must_file
         -- writable_potential_claimer_did_file: potential_claimer_did_file
         -- writable_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund: false }
    -- answers: R.DependentAnswers {
         -- gross_income: gross_income
         -- writable_qr_support_test: qr_support
         -- tin_type: tin_type
         -- is_us_citizen_full_year: citizen
         -- writable_us_resident: us_resident
         -- writable_us_national: us_national
         -- writable_canada_mexico_resident: canada_mexico_resident
         -- tp_claims: tp_claims
         -- tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc: false
         -- disqualified_due_to_parental_custody: false }
  }
```

## The cases of issue #17

### Parent with gross income $5,049, supported over half: qualifying relative

IRC 152(d)(2)(C): a parent need not live with the filer. $5,049 is less than
$5,050 (Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.24).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestParentIncome5049:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestParentIncome5049:
  definition m.gross_income equals $5,049
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.qualifying_child
  assertion d.qr_relationship_test
  assertion not d.member_of_household_test
  assertion d.relationship_member_of_household_test
  assertion d.gross_income_test
  assertion d.qr_support_test
  assertion d.not_qualifying_child_test
  assertion d.qualifying_relative
  assertion d.qc_or_qr
  assertion d.citizen_or_resident_test
  assertion d.eligible_dependent
  assertion d.is_claimed_dependent
  assertion d.is_claimed_if_claimable
```

### The same parent with gross income $5,050: not a qualifying relative

"less than the exemption amount" (152(d)(1)(B)): exactly $5,050 fails.
Known-bad output rejected: every other test passes.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestParentIncome5050:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestParentIncome5050:
  definition m.gross_income equals $5,050
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.gross_income_test
  assertion d.relationship_member_of_household_test and d.qr_support_test
    and d.not_qualifying_child_test
  assertion not d.qualifying_relative
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
  assertion not d.is_claimed_dependent
  # Not claimable, so "claimed if claimable" holds
  assertion d.is_claimed_if_claimable
```

### Non-relative who lived with the filer all year: qualifying relative

IRC 152(d)(2)(H); Pub 501 p 18, "Example 1—return not required": an
unrelated friend who lived with you all year.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNonRelativeAllYear:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestNonRelativeAllYear:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.NoneOfTheAbove
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |1990-09-09|
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.qr_relationship_test
  assertion d.member_of_household_test
  assertion d.relationship_member_of_household_test
  assertion d.qualifying_relative
  assertion d.eligible_dependent
```

### Non-relative who lived with the filer 8 months: not a qualifying relative

8 months is `SixToElevenMonths`, not "all year". Known-bad output rejected.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNonRelativeEightMonths:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestNonRelativeEightMonths:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.NoneOfTheAbove
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |1990-09-09|
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.SixToElevenMonths
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.member_of_household_test
  assertion not d.relationship_member_of_household_test
  assertion d.gross_income_test and d.qr_support_test
  assertion not d.qualifying_relative
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
```

### A person who is the qualifying child of another taxpayer: not a qualifying relative

Pub 501 p 18, Not a Qualifying Child Test, Example 4 then Example 2: a
13-year-old grandchild who lived with the filer 5 months is not the filer's
qualifying child (residency), and lives the rest of the year with a parent
who must file and claims the child. The grandchild is that parent's
qualifying child, so not the filer's qualifying relative.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestQualifyingChildOfAnother:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestQualifyingChildOfAnother:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.GrandChildOrOtherDescendantOfChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2011-05-05|
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition m.gross_income equals $0
  definition m.could_be_qc_of_another equals true
  definition m.potential_claimer_must_file equals true
  definition m.potential_claimer_did_file equals true
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.qualifying_child
  assertion d.qualifying_relative_minus_not_qc_test
  assertion d.is_qualifying_child_of_another
  assertion not d.not_qualifying_child_test
  assertion not d.qualifying_relative
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
```

### The other taxpayer is not required to file and does not file

Pub 501 p 18, "Child of person not required to file a return": the same
grandchild, but the parent need not file and does not: the grandchild is not
anyone else's qualifying child and is the filer's qualifying relative.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestQualifyingChildOfNonFiler:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestQualifyingChildOfNonFiler:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.GrandChildOrOtherDescendantOfChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2011-05-05|
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition m.gross_income equals $0
  definition m.could_be_qc_of_another equals true
  definition m.potential_claimer_must_file equals false
  definition m.potential_claimer_did_file equals false
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.is_qualifying_child_of_another
  assertion d.not_qualifying_child_test
  assertion d.qualifying_relative
  assertion d.eligible_dependent
```

### No TIN: not an eligible dependent

A 10-year-old child who is the filer's qualifying child but has no SSN, ITIN
or ATIN (Pub 501 pp 22-23). Known-bad output rejected: the same child with an
ATIN is eligible.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoTin:
  m scope MkMember
  m2 scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest
  internal d2 content R.DependentTest

scope TestNoTin:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2014-01-20|
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition m.tin_type equals R.TinType.NoTin
  definition m2.relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition m2.date_of_birth equals |2014-01-20|
  definition m2.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition m2.tin_type equals R.TinType.Atin
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  definition d2 equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m2.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion d.qualifying_child
  assertion d.qc_or_qr
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent_minus_filer_information
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
  assertion not d.is_claimed_dependent
  assertion d2.eligible_dependent
  assertion d2.is_claimed_dependent
```

### Adopted child who is not a citizen, resident or national

IRC 152(b)(3)(B); Pub 501 p 11, Exception for adopted child. A 6-year-old
adopted child who is a citizen and resident of another country (not Canada
or Mexico), lived with the filer all year; the filer is a U.S. citizen. The
exception applies. Known-bad outputs rejected: if the filer is not a citizen
or national, or the child lived with the filer only 8 months, it does not.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAdoptedChildException:
  m scope MkMember
  m_part scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest
  internal d_noncitizen_filer content R.DependentTest
  internal d_part_year content R.DependentTest

scope TestAdoptedChildException:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.AdoptedChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2018-02-14|
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition m.citizen equals false
  definition m.tin_type equals R.TinType.Atin
  definition m_part.relationship equals Q.Relationship.AdoptedChild
  definition m_part.date_of_birth equals |2018-02-14|
  definition m_part.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.SixToElevenMonths
  definition m_part.citizen equals false
  definition m_part.tin_type equals R.TinType.Atin
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  definition d_noncitizen_filer equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: false }
  definition d_part_year equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m_part.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion d.qualifying_child
  assertion d.child_is_adopted
  assertion not d.us_resident and not d.us_national
    and not d.canada_mexico_resident
  assertion d.adopted_child_exception
  assertion d.citizen_or_resident_test
  assertion d.citizen_or_us_resident_test
  assertion d.eligible_dependent
  assertion not d_noncitizen_filer.adopted_child_exception
  assertion not d_noncitizen_filer.citizen_or_resident_test
  assertion not d_noncitizen_filer.eligible_dependent
  # 8 months: still a qualifying child (over half the year), but the
  # exception needs the whole year
  assertion d_part_year.qualifying_child
  assertion not d_part_year.adopted_child_exception
  assertion not d_part_year.eligible_dependent
```

## Further cases

### Child living in Mexico (Pub 501 p 18, Child in Canada or Mexico)

A 6-year-old child, not a U.S. citizen, living in Mexico with the filer's
parent who is not a taxpayer: not a qualifying child (residency), but a
qualifying relative, and passes the citizen or resident test as a resident
of Mexico. Not `citizen_or_us_resident_test` (the CTC/ODC test).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestChildInMexico:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestChildInMexico:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2018-07-01|
  definition m.gross_income equals $0
  definition m.citizen equals false
  definition m.canada_mexico_resident equals true
  definition m.tin_type equals R.TinType.Itin
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.qualifying_child
  assertion d.qualifying_relative
  assertion d.canada_mexico_resident
  assertion not d.citizen_or_us_resident_test
  assertion d.citizen_or_resident_test
  assertion d.eligible_dependent
```

### A filer who can be claimed as a dependent claims no one (IRC 152(b)(1))

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFilerIsDependent:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestFilerIsDependent:
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: true
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion d.qualifying_relative
  assertion d.eligible_dependent_minus_filer_information
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
  assertion not d.is_claimed_dependent
  assertion d.is_claimed_if_claimable
```

### Married parent filing jointly (IRC 152(b)(2))

The parent files a joint return with their spouse (not only for a refund):
still a qualifying relative, but not a dependent.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMarriedParentJointReturn:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestMarriedParentJointReturn:
  definition m.married equals true
  definition m.writable_joint_return equals true
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion d.qualifying_relative
  assertion not d.qc.joint_return_test
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
```

### Eligible but not claimed

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEligibleNotClaimed:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestEligibleNotClaimed:
  definition m.tp_claims equals false
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion d.eligible_dependent
  assertion not d.is_claimed_dependent
  assertion not d.is_claimed_if_claimable
```

### DF-BUG(15): the filer's own qualifying child is not a qualifying relative

Pub 501 p 18, Not a Qualifying Child Test, Example 1: a 22-year-old student
child who lives with the filer and meets all the qualifying child tests "isn't
your qualifying relative", even with gross income under $5,050 and over half
support from the filer. DF says qualifying relative; we say no. The child is
a dependent either way.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestOwnQualifyingChildNotQualifyingRelative:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestOwnQualifyingChildNotQualifyingRelative:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2002-04-11|
  definition m.full_time_student equals true
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion d.qualifying_child
  assertion d.not_qualifying_child_test
  assertion d.qualifying_relative_minus_not_qc_test
  assertion not d.qualifying_relative
  assertion d.qc_or_qr
  assertion d.eligible_dependent
```

### DF-BUG(16): an older sibling who is a parent's qualifying child

The filer, born 2004-03-01, is 20. Their sibling, born 2003-01-10, is 21, a
full-time student, and lived with the filer 8 months; the sibling had $2,000
of gross income and the filer paid over half their support. The sibling fails
the age test for the filer (not younger, IRC 152(c)(3)(A)), so DF never asks
whether the sibling is someone else's qualifying child. The sibling is the
qualifying child of their parent, who must file: under 152(d)(1)(D) the
sibling is not the filer's qualifying relative. DF says qualifying relative.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestOlderSiblingQualifyingChildOfParent:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestOlderSiblingQualifyingChildOfParent:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Sibling
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2003-01-10|
  definition m.full_time_student equals true
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.SixToElevenMonths
  definition m.gross_income equals $2,000
  definition m.could_be_qc_of_another equals true
  definition m.potential_claimer_must_file equals true
  definition m.potential_claimer_did_file equals true
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |2004-03-01|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.qc.age_test
  assertion not d.qualifying_child
  assertion not d.ask_about_qc_of_another
  # DF's value: the gated answer is ignored
  assertion not d.is_qualifying_child_of_another
  # The statute: the answer counts
  assertion not d.not_qualifying_child_test
  assertion d.qualifying_relative_minus_not_qc_test
  assertion not d.qualifying_relative
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
```

### The household

Three members: the parent of the first case (claimed), a non-relative who
lived 8 months (not eligible), and a child with no TIN (not eligible).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHousehold:
  parent scope MkMember
  lodger scope MkMember
  child scope MkMember
  internal h content R.Dependents

scope TestHousehold:
  definition lodger.relationship equals Q.Relationship.NoneOfTheAbove
  definition lodger.date_of_birth equals |1990-09-09|
  definition lodger.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.SixToElevenMonths
  definition child.relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition child.date_of_birth equals |2014-01-20|
  definition child.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition child.tin_type equals R.TinType.NoTin
  definition h equals
    output of R.Dependents with {
      -- members: [parent.member; lodger.member; child.member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion number of h.results = 3
  assertion h.claimed_dependents_count = 1
```

### DF-BUG(16), the other side: a "yes" the statute rules out is ignored

A 9-year-old child who lived with the filer all year but provided over half
of their own support. They fail the support test of IRC 152(c)(1)(D), so they
are nobody's qualifying child, whatever the answer to "Is the dependent the
qualifying child of any other taxpayer?" (here yes, with a claimer who must
file, as in the oracle scenario `single-50k`). DF agrees (it never reads the
answer behind its gate).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestOwnSupportChildCannotBeAnyonesQualifyingChild:
  m scope MkMember
  internal d content R.DependentTest

scope TestOwnSupportChildCannotBeAnyonesQualifyingChild:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2015-09-09|
  definition m.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition m.own_support equals true
  definition m.could_be_qc_of_another equals true
  definition m.potential_claimer_must_file equals true
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion not d.qc.qc_support_test
  assertion not d.could_be_qualifying_child_of_some_taxpayer
  assertion d.not_qualifying_child_test
  # Fails the qualifying relative support test too: not a dependent
  assertion not d.qr_support_test
  assertion not d.qualifying_relative
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
```
